WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:05.390
The Season 5 finale of Arrow brought back
a bunch of fan favourite characters for an

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:09.710
epic showdown on Lian Yu and culminated in
an explosive cliffhanger.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.770
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video I want to take a look at

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:18.770
that Season 5 cliffhanger ending and see if
we can figure out who survived and who's returning

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.070
for Season 6.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.120
A quick reminder that my Arrowverse giveaway
is still running, so, for a chance to win

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.850
any of these Arrow, Flash or Supergirl Funko
Pops, subscribe and leave a comment with your

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.770
thoughts on the finale or Season 6.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.420
And just be aware that, obviously, there are
spoilers ahead if you're not up-to-date yet

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.420
with Arrow.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.129
So, this season Prometheus was certainly the
villain we've been looking for on Arrow, always

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:42.839
ten steps ahead of Oliver.

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:47.540
I really enjoyed Josh Segarra's performance
and his character was so irredeemably bad

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.230
that he even killed himself at the end hoping
to destroy Oliver's life by setting off the

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.499
bombs on Lian Yu to kill almost everyone that
Ollie cared about.

00:00:56.499 --> 00:01:00.940
As shocking as this was, this is, of course,
a comic book show and unless we see bodies

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.690
dead and buried, and even sometimes then,
it's hard to believe that they are all really

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.690
dead.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.080
On top of that, various characters that were
on the island at the end have already been

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.870
confirmed for Season 6 by the showrunners,
so let's examine who probably made it and

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.920
how they survived.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.020
Actress Katie Cassidy has already been confirmed
to return as Black Siren for Season 6 and,

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.650
given she was working with Prometheus, it's
quite likely she was aware of the bombs that

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:29.600
he'd set on the island, so she probably had
a means of getting off the island already

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.600
arranged.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.270
As Black Siren is coming back as a regular
next season, I wonder whether she could even

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.920
get a main villain role, if not for the whole
season, then perhaps at least initially?

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.430
And actors Juliana Harkavy and Rick Gonzalez
who play Dinah and Rene are also confirmed

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.340
as returning for Season 6.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:51.090
In the finale, we finally see Dinah validated
as the new Black Canary by Quentin Lance,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.140
which is nice because Dinah was the original
Black Canary in the comics before Laurel Lance

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.140
took on the mantle.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.320
But how did she, Wild Dog and the others survive
all those bombs?

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.620
Remember, Oliver says to Felicity there's
an Argus supply ship on the Eastern side of

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.849
the island, but that appears to be just minutes
before the bombs go off, so it seems unlikely

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:11.829
they could have made it there in time.

00:02:11.829 --> 00:02:16.069
However, let's not forget that Slade Wilson
is with them, and he knows Lian Yu well and

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:20.319
has just spent many years locked up in a reinforced
supermax prison on the island.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:25.170
So, I suspect Slade probably took as many
of them as he could to the safety of the Argus

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.709
prison bunker.

00:02:26.709 --> 00:02:30.629
Speaking of Deathstroke, given that in the
finale Oliver gives Slade Wilson a file with

00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:35.239
information on his son Joe, it seems unlikely
that the show would open up this thread without

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:39.129
exploring it further down the road, which
suggests that there are possible storylines

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:41.360
ahead about Slade looking for his son.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.290
Now, Manu Bennett is currently busy with other
roles, so whether he will return or how much

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.340
he could return for Season 6 is still unsure.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.849
Deathstroke was a great character when he
was a regular on the show and with the finale

00:02:52.849 --> 00:02:57.450
cameo of Oliver's mother Moira, who Slade
killed in Season 2, it would be amazing to

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.430
see Deathstroke return and further redeem
himself next season.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:06.200
Felicity, Diggle, Thea, Curtis, Quentin and
Nyssa were also with Slade, Dinah and Rene

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.920
at the end, and obviously it wouldn't be a
good move for the show to kill off these main

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.859
characters in between seasons.

00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:15.861
I suspect most of them made it to safety with
Slade, but there's always a chance we get

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:19.700
to see a few of them picked off in the opening
episode of season 6.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.200
For example, Thea has had a lot less to do
this season, so you could argue that she'd

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:28.459
be the most obvious one to go, however, I
feel she won't be killed off on the island,

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:31.609
especially as Merlyn may have given his life
to save hers.

00:03:31.609 --> 00:03:35.980
But could the show pull a similar move to
what The Flash did this season with HR and

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.340
Tracy, in other words, did they rekindle the
romance between Felicity and Oliver as a way

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.640
to raise the stakes for her character before
possibly killing her off?

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.480
After all, Prometheus did say to Oliver, 'it's
gonna be lonely without mom and Felicity',

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.269
just before he blew up the island.

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:54.689
Or, given the fact that there's little audience
attachment to the character, maybe it will

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:58.669
be Samantha, the mother of Oliver's son, William,
who doesn't make it off Lian Yu.

00:03:58.669 --> 00:04:02.910
A couple of baddies whose fate is less certain
would be Evelyn and Talia.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:07.780
Evelyn was last seen still locked up in the
cage and Talia had been knocked out by Nyssa.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.200
Though you can never totally count out a character
who's got the name al-Ghul!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:17.470
Now, let's not forget about another teased-but-not-seen
death during the finale: Malcolm Merlyn.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.930
Merlyn took Thea's place after she stepped
on a landmine and sent her away with the others

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.150
after Digger Harkness, aka Captain Boomerang,
and his gang caught up with them.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:30.620
Thea then saw an explosion in the distance
and assumed Merlyn had died, but remember

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:35.200
Slade Wilson's words to Boomerang earlier
in the episode: "Assumption is the mother

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.470
of all failures".

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:41.160
However, John Barrowman, who plays Merlyn,
made a Facebook video shortly after the episode

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:45.310
finished, saying that he won't be back for
Season 6 and that he's very sad to be leaving

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.310
the Arrowverse.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:50.650
So, it looks like this is the end for Merlyn
then, but at least he was able to redeem himself

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:53.270
somewhat by sacrificing himself for his daughter.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.800
Of course, we're still in comic book territory
here so it's possible that the showrunners

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:03.370
decided to have Merlyn's death off-screen
to leave things more open for the future.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:07.880
After all, Merlyn was looking pretty cocky
when Boomerang turned up and it's not unfeasible

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:12.030
that he could have pulled Boomerang onto the
landmine while launching himself as far away

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:14.170
as he could from the explosion.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:17.150
And let's not forget this green vial that
he wears around his neck.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:22.330
If that contains waters from the Lazarus Pit,
then he could use it to heal any major injuries

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:23.690
from the blast.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:28.120
Malcolm has returned from apparent death before
and has dubbed himself the Magician both in

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:33.830
the TV show and the comics so, even if he
did die, we can't absolutely rule out his

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:36.020
return, even if it's only in flashbacks.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:41.500
So, who do you think survived Lian Yu and
what did you think about the Arrow season

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.500
finale?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.180
Also, what would you like to see happen in
Season 6?

